Consider the following C++ function:

```cpp
unsigned int f(unsigned int n) {
    unsigned int b = 0;
    while (n) {
        b += n & 1;
        n >>= 1;
    }
    return b;
}
```

The function `f()` returns an int that represents the ______ in the binary representation of the positive integer `n`.

What is the output of the following C program?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
main() {
    int i, j, x = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 5; ++i)
        for (j = 0; j < i; ++j) {
            x += (i + j - 1);
            break;
        }
    printf("%d", x);
}
```
